clasped:
For then, it seemed, some grand blind Love came down,
And groped her out, and clasped her with a kiss;
She learnt God that way, and was beat for it

clamouring:
A day went by, a week went by. One day I heard it said:
'Men are clamouring, women, children, clamouring to be fed;
Men like famished dogs are howling in the streets for bread.'

clamorous:
And lively, like his father!’ one was keen
To get to work, and fill some clamorous mouths;
And one was tender for her dear goodman

clanging:
Thy fragrance now the factory's smell;
Too near for me the clanging bell;
A false light in the water shines

clasps:
The river sleeps beneath the sky,
And clasps the shadows to its breast;
The crescent moon shines dim on high;

granite and the ore in rocks;
a great band clasps your forehead
and its heavy twists of gold.

claw:
She searches for something,
Her withered claw
Tumbles the seaweed;

clashing:
Eagerly the crowd were waiting,
Loud the clashing sabres rang;
When between the gladiators

The iron clapper laughed aloud,
Like clashing wind and wave;
The bell cried out "Be strong and proud!"

clattah:
Come acrost de flo'.
Den dey comes a clattah
At de cabin do';

clasp'd:
One only daughter lives, and she the least;
The queen close clasp'd the daughter to her breast:
"Ye heav'nly pow'rs, ah spare me one," she cry'd,

clare:
And Nell was pale with pride;
My lord gazed long on pale Maude Clare
Or ever he kissed the bride.

clangour:
Prepared, at each emerging sense, to beat
And crash it out with clangour. I was weak;
I struggled for the posture of my soul

claudia's:
At the pale Penelope;
Cutting in on Claudia's dances;
Taking Iris out to tea.
